<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Gomes da Costa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1863–1929</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Gomes da Costa was a Portuguese general who launched the military coup of 28 May 1926 that overthrew the First Portuguese Republic. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> he had commanded a division of the Portuguese Expeditionary Corps in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>. After heading the new regime for only a few weeks, he was ousted in July 1926 by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscar-carmona">Óscar Carmona</a> and sent into exile in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azores">Azores</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-gomes-da-costa.jpg" alt="Manuel Gomes da Costa" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographia Vasques · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Manuel_Gomes_da_Costa_(1918)_-_Photographia_Vasques.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
